        {
          "id": "india-semicon-2-ecms-approvals-2026-11-06",
          "headline": "Semicon 2.0 portal opens; 12 more component plants worth ₹7,503 crore approved",
          "summary": "IT Minister Ashwini Vaishnaw opened the Semicon 2.0 application portal, taking applications for chip equipment and materials, new fabs and packaging units under the ₹1.27 lakh crore programme. MeitY also cleared 12 more projects under the Electronics Components Manufacturing Scheme, worth ₹7,503 crore, expected to make ₹39,045 crore of output and create 7,127 direct jobs in seven states. Products include multilayer PCBs, relays, copper foil, cathode material and specialty ceramics.",
          "why_it_matters": "It pushes India beyond phone assembly into the parts and materials that go inside electronics and batteries.",
