          "id": "currency-us-jobs-dollar-2026-11-06",
          "headline": "Dollar ends with its best day since June as traders bet on a December Fed hike",
          "summary": "Update: after Friday's strong jobs report, the dollar index closed about 0.7% higher near 102.3, its biggest one-day gain since mid-June, and the euro had its worst day since early October. Markets now price about a 78% chance of a quarter-point Fed hike at the December 8-9 meeting, up from about 67% on Thursday. St Louis Fed chief Alberto Musalem said inflation is still his top worry.",
