          "summary": "US tech stocks recovered part of Thursday's crash: the Nasdaq closed up 1.1% at 24,579 and the S&P 500 rose 0.3% to 7,377, while the Dow fell 0.5% to 51,286. Chipmakers led the bounce, with AMD up about 9% and Micron about 5% after a 17% drop. Markets elsewhere fared worse: Korea's Kospi fell 6% and the FTSE 100 lost 1%, on fears that the Democrats' midterm win will slow AI spending.",
